                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2802644,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "It's hard to choose, but Alive and Kicking is definitely worth mentioning. You won't have heard of the writer as it's her first book, which is really impressive. It's basically the teenage diary of a boy from Somalia who comes to live in The UK. It deals with the serious issue of immigration and all the challenges the boy has to face at school and with the language barrier, etcetera. Usually, books like this are quite sad, but this one actually made me cry with laughter.",
